{
  "abstract": "Which roots of the Coxeter polynomial are algebraic conjugates of the Salem spectral radius, and which are roots of unity? For every E_m star tree of rank m >= 10, the three new compared theorems (23)-(25) answer this question for the explicit Coxeter matrix. The seven possible orders 2, 3, 5, 8, 12, 18, 30 are selected by rank congruences. Dividing out one copy of each selected cyclotomic polynomial gives exactly the minimal polynomial of the spectral radius over Q. In particular, it has the full degree m precisely for m = 2, 10, 16, 20, 22, 26 or 28 modulo 30. This formalizes Gross-Hironaka-McMullen, Theorem 1.1 in the hyperbolic range and Corollary 1.4. The proof uses cyclotomic conjugacies and the simple-root count for the Salem family. For example, rank 38 gives the factor Phi_30 and a Salem number of degree 30. This version also includes all 22 version-2 statements on the degree-12 compositum of the cubic and quartic Mahler minimizers, its exact Mahler measure and minimal recurrence, the Bedford-Kim plastic family, Lehmer's polynomial and the Coxeter bridge.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Stephanie Alexander"
    }
